If You and Fish Audio have signed a separate written agreement covering the Fish Audio Materials, that agreement governs to the extent it conflicts with this Agreement.

## V. DEFINITIONS

**"Affiliate(s)"** means any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with the subject entity; for purposes of this definition, "control" means direct or indirect ownership or control of more than 50% of the voting interests of the subject entity.

**"Agreement"** means this Fish Audio Community License Agreement, Version 1.0 (also referred to as the "Fish Audio Community License, Version 1.0" or "FACL v1.0").

**"Annual Revenue"** and **"Revenue Threshold"** have the meanings given in Section III(a), and **"Hosted Service"** has the meaning given in Section III(c).

**"Derivative Work(s)"** means (a) any derivative work of the Fish Audio Materials as recognized by U.S. copyright laws and (b) any modification of a Model, including any model initialized from all or part of a Model's weights (such as fine-tuned, quantized, merged, and low-rank adaptation ("LoRA") models), whether or not it was trained using output of a Model or Derivative Work. Derivative Works do not include the output of any Model or Derivative Work, or any other model trained or distilled using such output.

**"Documentation"** means any specifications, manuals, model cards, documentation, and other written information that Fish Audio makes available under this Agreement related to the Software or Models.

**"Fish Audio"** or **"we"** means 39 AI, INC. and its Affiliates.

**"Model(s)"** means the machine-learning models, including trained model weights and other elements of the foregoing, that Fish Audio makes available under this Agreement, including Fish Audio Drama 3 and, solely for use with Fish Audio Drama 3 and its Derivative Works, the audio codec that Fish Audio provides for use with Fish Audio Drama 3 (including the copy of that codec distributed with Fish Audio S2-Pro).

**"Software"** means Fish Audio's proprietary software made available under this Agreement now or in the future, including the Fish Speech source code (https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-speech).

**"Fish Audio Materials"** means, collectively, the Models, Software and Documentation (and any portion or combination thereof) made available under this Agreement. Model weights that Fish Audio makes available under a different license (for example, the Fish Audio S2-Pro weights under the Fish Audio Research License) are not Fish Audio Materials, even if the Software can run them, except as stated in the definition of Model(s) for the audio codec.

**"Trade Control Laws"** means any applicable U.S. and non-U.S. export control and trade sanctions laws and regulations.
